From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:04:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 177/178] DeepSeek V4.1 WO-A quantizes its input as the
 reference does

DeepSeek's reference (2026-10-12 revision, for both V4.1 Flash checkpoints, the
original and 1017) quantizes the attention output before the grouped WO-A
einsum, in the attention and the DSpark drafter attention alike:
act_quant(o, 32, "ue8m0", inplace=True), each 32-value block to E4M3 with a
UE8M0 scale and back to BF16. The W8A16 GEMM kept BF16 activations, as the
earlier reference did.

The W8A16 kernels (used only by WO-A) now quantize each activation tile as
they load it (_reference_roundtrip: _reference_cast's amax floor and exponent,
E4M3, times 2^e, exact in BF16), before expanding the weights and the MMA;
block_K is a multiple of 32 and each group's K starts on a block, so a tile
holds whole reference blocks, and split and in-kernel paths agree bit for bit.
No extra pass over o. The BF16-activation path is gone.

Tests: the projection against FP64 on act_quant's values; the quantizing
kernel on x and on x already through TileKernels' per_token_cast (byte-
identical to act_quant) give the same bits, below the amax floor too.
